    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88-a1">

                <pb facs="0160" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg153"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 88]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Commander O’Neil.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States,<lb/>Nicaragua, Costa Rica, and
                                Salvador</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August 2, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Commander <hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Neil</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">U. S. S. Marblehead, Bluefields:</hi></p>
                <p>The Nicaraguan Government had chartered, as I learn, the steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Yulu</hi>, belonging to a company of Americans, to carry
                    troops from Grey Town to Bluefields. The President desires to know if this is
                    contrary to your order commanding the neutrality of American citizens. Please
                    answer in care of Consul Braida, Grey Town.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Baker</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
